      "text": "The foci of the ellipse lie along the major axis a distance $c$ from the center.  The equation of the ellipse is $(x^2/a^2)+(y^2/b^2)=1$, where $a=5$, and thus $c=\\sqrt{a^2-b^2}=\\sqrt{25-16}=3$.  The circle, centered at a focus of the ellipse, will tangent to the ellipse at its minor axis; thus, with radius $r$, we have $b^2=r^2+r^2=2r^2$, and $2r=8\\Rightarrow \\boxed{r=4}$. The answer is 4",
